            390.0,
            888.0,
            498.0
          ],
          "source_type": "text",
          "source_sentence": "The FT-IR spectra of polymers (Table 1) show that all the spectra have the stretching vibration for the C=O group $( 1 , 6 5 3 { - } 1 , 6 5 7 \\ \\mathrm { c m } ^ { - 1 } )$and the N–H group $( 3 , 3 9 4 - 3 , 3 9 8 ~ \\mathrm { c m } ^ { - 1 } )$in the acylamide linkage, the stretching vibration for CN group $( 2 , 2 3 1 - 2 , 2 3 3 ~ \\mathrm { c m } ^ { - 1 } )$, the stretching vibration for $\\mathrm { C - N } ( 1 , 2 4 4 - 1 , 2 4 7 ~ \\mathrm { c m } ^ { - 1 } )$, and the stretching vibration for the ether group asymmetrical vibration of Ar–O–Ar (1,241– $1 { , } 2 4 2 \\ \\mathrm { c m } ^ { - 1 } )$"
        }
      ],
      "confidence": {
        "score": 0.9
      }
